{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKh6s1ziaWUe8NPU5zxk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NtW8MnoJ4tgHZB3gM3BEkL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/work/.ard/158/triage-lead.md","content":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nA small bug fix in the redactor: the env var that selects the agent auth mode holds a mode name rather than a credential, yet it is collected into the secret set, so a spurious warning is logged on every serve start and close-out. The change is confined to the redact package (the name-pattern match in FromEnviron in internal/redact/secrets.go) plus a test, so only the engineer needs to plan it.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: choose how to exclude the mode variable from the environment-based secret collection (e.g. an explicit non-secret allowlist) while keeping the real credential variables redacted, and specify the test that asserts no warning for it.\n- worker engineer: narrow code change in internal/redact with a unit test.\n\n## Open issues\n- The secret-name match is a broad pattern that includes AUTH, so other non-secret variables with that substring would behave the same way. The planner should keep the exclusion narrow so no real credential stops being redacted.\n- An earlier triage run for this issue failed at the push step in the controller, not in routing. A maintainer may want to confirm that push problem is resolved.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4539,"cache_read_input_tokens":12917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4539},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f9ccb6-507b-4cd7-a4be-cc2d43bbb5a0","uuid":"23b13d5f-6728-4167-ba7a-ffbb2efb792b","timestamp":"2026-11-23T10:21:00.164Z","request_id":"req_011ChKh6rsoiy2XvXFi7VoBp"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NtW8MnoJ4tgHZB3gM3BEkL","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /work/.ard/158/triage-lead.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f9ccb6-507b-4cd7-a4be-cc2d43bbb5a0","uuid":"dbacbe76-c6d6-4f01-a443-c38e8d6fc56b","timestamp":"2026-11-23T10:21:00.175Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/work/.ard/158/triage-lead.md","content":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nA small bug fix in the redactor: the env var that selects the agent auth mode holds a mode name rather than a credential, yet it is collected into the secret set, so a spurious warning is logged on every serve start and close-out. The change is confined to the redact package (the name-pattern match in FromEnviron in internal/redact/secrets.go) plus a test, so only the engineer needs to plan it.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: choose how to exclude the mode variable from the environment-based secret collection (e.g. an explicit non-secret allowlist) while keeping the real credential variables redacted, and specify the test that asserts no warning for it.\n- worker engineer: narrow code change in internal/redact with a unit test.\n\n## Open issues\n- The secret-name match is a broad pattern that includes AUTH, so other non-secret variables with that substring would behave the same way. The planner should keep the exclusion narrow so no real credential stops being redacted.\n- An earlier triage run for this issue failed at the push step in the controller, not in routing. A maintainer may want to confirm that push problem is resolved.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NtW8MnoJ4tgHZB3gM3BEkL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKh7HVtwJYyaimbL6Byx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #158 as **done**: the triage engineer will plan it and the engineer worker will implement it. The routing is written to `.ard/158/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Cause:** The redactor treats any environment variable whose name contains `AUTH` as a secret (pattern in `internal/redact/secrets.go:25`). `ARD_AGENT_AUTH` matches, but it only holds a short mode name, so it fails the 8-character minimum and triggers the warning on every start.\n- **Scope:** The fix is a narrow change in `internal/redact` plus a test, and it doesn't change user-visible behaviour or a public interface. So only `triage:engineer` is needed, and no extra review is requested.\n- **Open issues for a maintainer:**\n  - The name pattern is broad, so other harmless variables with `AUTH` in the name would hit the same warning. The fix should be narrow so that no real credential stops being redacted.\n  - An earlier run of this same routing step failed when the controller tried to push to GitHub, not in the routing itself. It's worth checking that the push problem is fixed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":745,"cache_read_input_tokens":17456,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":745},"output_tokens":367,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f9ccb6-507b-4cd7-a4be-cc2d43bbb5a0","uuid":"e5a99188-bbe5-494b-a550-2726f4bb473f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T10:21:04.141Z","request_id":"req_011ChKh7HMU1SgkkcirZXgSx"}
